// PURPOSE: Mark the Dart-side entry point of the Android ink package and state exactly how far
//          the implementation has got, for the same reason as the iOS package: a caller must not
//          be able to mistake scaffolding for a working pen.
// INPUTS: None.
// OUTPUTS: A library with no public API yet.
// KEYWORDS: ink-native, android, inkview, spike-s2, no-api-yet, honest-scaffold
//
// Present today: the Kotlin plugin scaffolding generated by `flutter create` —
// `InkNativeAndroidPlugin` under android/src/main/kotlin, the Gradle build, and the manifest —
// registered through the `flutter.plugin` section of pubspec.yaml.
//
// Not present: the Dart class implementing InkNativePlatform, and the InkView itself with its
// coalesced and predicted event handling. Both are spike S2 work; the latency they are measured
// against is the 45 ms p95 S Pen threshold.
//
// No stub is provided on purpose. See ink_native_ios/lib/ink_native_ios.dart for why an empty
// implementation would be worse than an absent one.

/// Android ink implementation, backed by a custom InkView. No public API yet.
library;
